        </h2>
        <p
          class="text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300"
        >
          A cylinder is a right circular geometric solid with two parallel
          circular bases of equal radius. The formula for the volume of a
          cylinder is:
        </p>
        <div
          class="rounded-2xl bg-blue-50/60 p-4 dark:bg-blue-950/30 border border-blue-100 dark:border-blue-900/40 text-xs sm:text-sm font-mono text-blue-900 dark:text-blue-200"
        >
          Volume = π × (Radius)² × Height = π × (Diameter / 2)² × Height
        </div>
        <p
          class="text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300"
        >
          When using diameter, remember to divide by 2 before squaring: <code
            class="font-mono bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded"
